From 9bc3b1295cba999a1ba2ab0b496aa973a4964f22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cpkt9762 <cpkt9762@163.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:28:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] docs(skills): extend the save-acknowledgement exception to
 the DSH adapter

Fork-only: expand the existing narrow native mem_save exception from Pi to Pi and DSH. Preserve every authority, bounded replay, cancellation and UUID telemetry clause unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6.1-sol) <noreply@openai.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 skills/plugin-thin/SKILL.md | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/skills/plugin-thin/SKILL.md b/skills/plugin-thin/SKILL.md
index 2ba39dc..d5fd2a5 100644
--- a/skills/plugin-thin/SKILL.md
+++ b/skills/plugin-thin/SKILL.md
@@ -27,9 +27,9 @@ Use this skill when:
 
 ---
 
-## Narrow Pi Exception: Observation-Save Acknowledgement Recovery
+## Narrow Pi and DSH Exception: Observation-Save Acknowledgement Recovery
 
-`plugin/pi` native `mem_save` may resolve only an ambiguous acknowledgement because
+`plugin/pi` and `plugin/dsh` native `mem_save` may resolve only an ambiguous acknowledgement because
 the Go server cannot observe that a client lost one. Go remains the sole authority
 for the durable ledger, canonical fingerprint, validation, conflicts, tombstones,
 retention, and mutation effects.
